;
;Both RexxDoor and RexxDebug are Re-ENTRANT programs , you may place them
;in the AmigaDos resident list by doing either of the following:
;
; 
;   resident RexxDoor bbs:utils/rexxdebug
;   resident RexxDoor bbs:utils/rexxdoor
;
;   NOTE!!: rexxdebug can only be invoke by /X if it's name is rexxdoor
;           or if it is in the AmigaDos resident list as rexxdoor.
;
;REXXDEBUG 2.0 this is an AIM interface designed with the AIM developer
;              in mind. Only a developer or someone who suspects one of
;              the AIM scripts are faultly, should be running this, as this
;              interface will report to you any invalid commands it receives
;              from the AIM script.
;
;
;
;REXXDOOR 2.0 removed the AIM debug routines and placed them into a 
;             seperate AIM interface known as RexxDebug
;            
;             REXXDOOR 2.0 requires that sys:rexxc/rx is resident
;             in memory. procedure for this is as follows:
;
;             resident rx sys:rexxc/rx
;
;--------------
;REXXDOOR 1.9 beta release, utilizes registerized parameters vs
;stack parameters.
;
;Notice this is a special release, and will display invalid AIM commands
;to the screen as the rexx scripts is in progress. This will help isolate
;why certain doors give you problems over others.
;
;Also this rexxdoor maybe made resident, it currently looks for RX not 
;sys:rexxc/rx so this means you can make RX resident as well. if you wish
;to make this rexxdoor resident and RX resident please add the following
;to your user-startup
;

resident rx sys:rexxc/rx
resident rexxdoor bbs:utils/rexxdoor
;
;
;all rexx doors add the tooltype RESIDENT to the mod/door icons
;
;
; NOTE: you can execute this script to install rx and rexxdoor resident